messages:
Lena (Customer): Hi team — embedding Redwood in our iOS app. After a few hundred users hit the widget we start seeing intermittent 429s and occasional 503s. No code change on our side between success and the spike. Logs: `embed-init: failed preflight 429 token_fanout`
Maya (CS): Thanks Lena — can you paste SDK version and where tokens are minted? Also are you using ephemeral tokens directly in the client?
Lena (Customer): sdk-js v1.12.0, we mint ephemerals from our auth service and hand them to the client. We did a push that increased websocket reconnects (mobile), could that cause fanout?
OnboardBot: automated alert: customer-rate-window exceeded (429) — 11 hits/minute for same token origin. See docs: https://docs.redwood.ai/rate-limits
Rafael (Infra Eng): Likely a preflight/token fanout problem. If many clients request fresh ephemerals simultaneously you can get a thundering preflight. Two quick checks: (1) confirm ephemeral TTL — <20s can cause churn; (2) check whether clients request a preflight per tab/reconnect instead of reusing cached token.
Jo (Solutions Eng): Short-term workaround: coalesce preflight calls on the client and add a tiny randomized delay before minting/fetching tokens. Example (JS):
```js
// debounce preflight + jitter
let preflightPending = false;
function requestPreflight() {
  if (preflightPending) return;
  preflightPending = true;
  const jitter = Math.random() * 250; // ms
  setTimeout(async () => {
    await fetch('/auth/get-ephemeral');
    preflightPending = false;
  }, 100 + jitter);
}
```
Maya (CS): Also as a short mitigation we can temporarily raise the customer's preflight quota for 24 hours or route them to a lower-capacity model variant to avoid 503s while they stabilize. I can authorize a 24h bump if you want, Lena.
Lena (Customer): A quota bump would help while we deploy the debounce. ETA for client change: 2 hours. Can we get a rollback plan if quota bump causes cost issues?
Rafael (Infra Eng): We'll monitor token origin and add a temporary circuit-breaker on our side: if we see > 5 concurrent outstanding preflight requests from same origin, we reply with `Retry-After: 1s` and a hint header `X-RW-Advice: coalesce`. Also check response headers for `X-RateLimit-Reset` to implement smarter backoff.
Jo (Solutions Eng): Extra tip: on mobile, persist ephemeral for session-level reuse (not per WS reconnect). If you must refresh often, proxy the refresh through your server and return the same ephemeral to simultaneous clients for a short window.
Maya (CS): Action items: 1) Maya -> temporary 24h quota bump (if Lena confirms) 2) Lena -> deploy debounce + session cache (ETA 2h) 3) Rafael -> add monitor for token-origin fanout and circuit-breaker rule (in prod by EOD) 4) Jo -> provide sample server-proxy pattern and small backoff lib snippet.
Lena (Customer): Confirmed — please apply quota bump. I'll ping when client deploy is done. Thanks! :thumbsup:
Maya (CS): Done — applied 24h preflight quota bump and flagged for monitoring. Please report if you see any more 429/503s.
Rafael (Infra Eng): I'll post a dashboard link in here once the monitor is live.
Jo (Solutions Eng): Posting server-proxy snippet in next message and a tiny package you can drop into the app. :rocket:
